<!--
  Paste into .github/copilot-instructions.md so Copilot Chat / Copilot
  Workspace picks it up as a workspace instruction.
-->

## Git commit and PR attribution

- Never add a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer naming Copilot or any other AI
  assistant to a commit message or PR description.
- Never add "Generated with Copilot", "AI-assisted", "AI-generated", or any
  other AI attribution, logo, or metadata to a commit message, PR title, PR
  description, or PR comment.
- Commits and PRs must read as 100% authored by the human user.

<!--
  Copilot's commit-message generation (the sparkle icon in the Source
  Control view) does not currently add co-author trailers by default, so
  the main risk is Copilot Chat/agent modes drafting a commit message that
  includes one when asked to write one "as if from an AI pair programmer".
  This instruction file plus the commit-msg hook cover both cases.
-->
